**Stub.** This page gathers the How-to section of each milestone. Each step opens the official page at the moment it is needed. The milestone pages say why each step matters and what the done check is.

The official order is wrist to base, because every wire passes down through the robot ([building instructions](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/assets/pdf/PAROL6_building_instructions.pdf#page=7), page 7).

## M1. Bench it

- [Stepper drivers](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/board/05-stepper-drivers/): driver orientation and heatsinks.
- [Electronics and wiring](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/build/electronics-and-wiring/) and [Connecting](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/04-installation/connecting/): supply polarity.
- [The test firmware](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/board/09-test-firmware/): `#IO`, `#LIMIT` and `#STOP`.

More: [M1 how-to](/lore/m1-bench-it#how-to).

## M2. One joint end to end

- [Building instructions](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/assets/pdf/PAROL6_building_instructions.pdf#page=20), pages 20 to 23 and 97 to 98.
- Firmware upload with an ST-Link and the adapter ([Firmware](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/board/08-firmware/)).
- The direction check ([Firmware and first run](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/build/firmware-and-first-run/), section 4) and [Jogging](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/05-operation/jogging/).

More: [M2 how-to](/lore/m2-one-joint#how-to).

## M3. The whole arm moves

- The building instructions, joint by joint.
- The wiring diagram and "Test before you close the base" ([Electronics and wiring](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/build/electronics-and-wiring/)).
- First power-on, direction fixes and homing ([Firmware and first run](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/build/firmware-and-first-run/)).
- Witness marks and [Mastering](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/05-operation/mastering/).

More: [M3 how-to](/lore/m3-whole-arm#how-to).

## M4. Pick and place

- Gripper setup and the homing offset for the tool ([Homing](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/05-operation/homing/); [End effectors](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/end-effectors/)).
- RBTscript programs ([Running programs](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/05-operation/running-programs/)).
- The [Python API](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/programming/02-python-api/).

More: [M4 how-to](/lore/m4-pick-and-place#how-to).

## M5 to M7

**Our design.** The official manual stops at pick-and-place. These steps are our own scripts on the [Python API](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/programming/02-python-api/), written as completion tasks: [M5 how-to](/lore/m5-touch-the-skiff#how-to), [M6 how-to](/lore/m6-patch-a-cable#how-to) and [M7 how-to](/lore/m7-play-it#how-to).

## Terms

- **building instructions**: the official assembly PDF. It builds the robot from the wrist to the base, because every wire passes down through it ([building instructions](https://docs.source-robotics.com/PAROL-docs/1.1/assets/pdf/PAROL6_building_instructions.pdf#page=7), page 7).
